Senior Contracts Manager &lt;p&gt;Senior Contracts Manager&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location – UK - Windsor/ Edinburgh / Ireland - Dublin &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Type of Work - Office&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Role Overview&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced and proactive Senior Contracts Manager to join the UKI Legal team. The role will support business growth and financial objectives by managing legal and commercial risk and enabling effective delivery of software and services to the NHS, and other UK &amp;amp; Ireland (UKI) healthcare and non-healthcare customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Contracts Manager will play a key role in managing contracts across their full lifecycle, working closely with the Legal, Sales, Delivery and Leadership teams to ensure contractual arrangements align with business objectives, governance requirements and public sector procurement norms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the senior contracts role in the UKI Legal team, the Senior Contracts Manager will generally be assigned the most complex, high-value and strategically significant matters. They must also operate with substantial autonomy within an agreed mandate, and help set standards, draft regional and global processes, and develop capability across the contracts function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be based in either InterSystems’ Windsor, Edinburgh, or Dublin offices and may require occasional domestic and international travel. Office location will be determined based on the successful candidate’s location. An office location that is not Windsor will require periodic attendance at the Windsor office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Responsibilities &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;– The role encompasses end-to-end contract lifecycle management, including pre-contract support, post-contract management, and risk and governance oversight.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pre-Contract Activities&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead legal team input into assigned tender and bid responses, particularly for NHS and other public sector procurements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, review and negotiate a range of customer and supplier contracts, ensuring alignment with business objectives, legal and commercial risk appetite, and applicable NHS and public sector requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide pragmatic and commercially focused contractual advice to support sales and project mobilisation activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Post-Contract Management&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take named, end-to-end ownership of a defined portfolio of client contracts, including high-value and complex contracts, holding accountability for commercial outcomes across the contract lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage contracts following signature, including business adherence to contractual obligations, change control processes and contract variations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the delivery and operations teams in the practical application and management of contractual obligations throughout the contract lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor contractual performance, compliance and key post-signature obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the management of third-party vendors/sub-contractors and suppliers, both local and global, as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Risk and Governance&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the implementation, day-to-day governance, administration and continuous improvement of regional and global AI-enabled legal support technologies, ensuring effective, compliant and business-aligned usage across the legal function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, assess and escalate legal and commercial risks to appropriate internal stakeholders and, where necessary, internal or external legal counsel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and ensure adherence to internal contract management and governance processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage ambiguity and develop practical, proportionate solutions to contractual and risk management challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Stakeholder Engagement&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear, practical guidance on contractual matters to colleagues at all levels, including the Legal, Sales, Delivery and Leadership teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and develop contract managers and other colleagues, setting standards and sharing best contract management practice across the global legal team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with local and international colleagues to resolve contractual issues efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Experience/Qualification Required &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 7-9 years proven, hands-on experience in high-value contract management, ideally within healthcare, IT, and/or the public sector. As a guide to applicants, evidence of a directly accountable portfolio TCV over £100M is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience of operating with autonomy on high-value, complex and strategically significant contracts, and of leading negotiations through to conclusion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong drafting, negotiation and analytical skills, with a pragmatic and commercially focused approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with digital workflow tools, document automation systems, and AI enabled legal support technologies to improve contract review speed, accuracy, consistency, and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience of legal operations processes, contract lifecycle management platforms and AI-enabled legal technologies is highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience of using UKI model form contracts and frameworks, with an understanding of government and NHS procurement laws and public sector contracting norms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify, define and articulate key commercial principles to support sound legal and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, including the ability to explain complex contractual issues to non-specialists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment, strong organisational skills and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively within cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree and/or postgraduate qualifications with a legal or commercial focus are preferred; relevant professional qualifications are welcomed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI-related regulatory environments such as the EU AI Act is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About InterSystems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;InterSystems, a creative data technology provider, delivers a unified foundation for next-generation applications for healthcare, finance, manufacturing, and supply chain customers in more than 80 countries. Our data platforms solve interoperability, speed, and scalability problems for large organizations around the globe to unlock the power of data and allow people to perceive data in imaginative ways. Established in 1978, InterSystems is committed to excellence through its 24×7 support for customers and partners around the world. Privately held and headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts, InterSystems has 38 offices in 28 countries worldwide. For more information, please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https://www.intersystems.com/&amp;amp;esheet=53379223&amp;amp;newsitemid=20230410005415&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=InterSystems.com&amp;amp;index=4&amp;amp;md5=3edf749fa33f5a2ac0c355c410576e90&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;1e721f69-f681-4067-9281-970e94b3ef11&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;InterSystems.com&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Disclaimer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;InterSystems may use AI tools for its internal operations including administrative tasks during recruitment (e.g., organizing candidate information). &amp;nbsp;InterSystems’ approach to AI is guided by the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.intersystems.com/ai-use-guidelines/&quot;&gt;InterSystems Responsible AI Guidelines&lt;/a&gt;. AI is not used to make or influence hiring decisions. All decisions are made by InterSystems employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates may use AI for CV or interview preparation, provided materials are truthful and reflect their own experience. &amp;nbsp;AI tools and third-party transcription services must not be used during interviews or assessments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that the use of wearable technology, including any AI-related tools or other technology-connected devices (such as META or Google smart glasses and/or wearables, and/or any similar devices), is&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;strictly prohibited&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;during the interview and screening process with InterSystems.&amp;nbsp; Any applicant who requires a wearable device or any type of technology support during the interview process as a reasonable accommodation under the ADA or applicable state or country laws and regulations must contact the InterSystems Human Resources Department&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;prior&lt;/em&gt; to attending or participating in any interview or screening process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Legal  Edinburgh; Windsor

Senior Branch Merchandiser &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Commerce is the global leader in licensed sports merchandise, operating a vertically integrated platform that designs, manufactures, and delivers officially licensed apparel, jerseys, headwear, and collectibles for major leagues, teams, and events worldwide. With more than 900 e-commerce sites and a global omnichannel presence across digital, in-venue, and retail, Fanatics Commerce reaches fans in over 180 countries and powers official fan experiences for many of the world&#39;s most iconic sports properties.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Fanatics, we bring our BOLD Leadership Principles to life every day - building championship teams, obsessing over fans, acting with entrepreneurial speed, and delivering with a determined and relentless mindset.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As we continue to scale our global platform, the Senior Branch Merchandiser will play a critical role in setting the branch merchandising strategy across retail stores and international locations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ROLE OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a newly created role that offers the opportunity to set the branch merchandising strategy and ownership structures across retail stores in the UK with scope to expand across additional international locations. The successful candidate will evolve and streamline the existing critical path — currently spread across multiple teams — into a cohesive approach to range planning, space planning, and allocation strategy, establishing clear processes across commercial functions. The Senior Branch Merchandiser delivers business and fan impact through BOLD leadership and execution excellence, leveraging data, automation, and AI-enabled insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HOW WILL YOU DRIVE IMPACT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success is measured by the ability to deliver results through BOLD capabilities and measurable outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team &amp;amp; Leadership Impact&lt;/strong&gt; (Build Championship Teams)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong working relationships and collaborate cross-functionally with Retail, Buying &amp;amp; Merchandising, Logistics, and Finance teams to ensure alignment and delivery against commercial objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with supply chain and logistics to forecast short-term retail dispatch and DC volumes, and to determine the best delivery day, method, and frequency for each store.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain buy-in at Senior Management level through excellent communication and influencing skills, presenting data-backed strategies and recommendations with confidence and clarity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the ownership structure and clear processes across the commercial functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fan &amp;amp; Customer Impact&lt;/strong&gt; (Obsessed with Fans)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver an optimised, balanced range for retail that meets and exceeds sales and margin targets, ensuring fans in every store have access to the right product at the right time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular store visits to gather market intelligence and competitor analysis, translating insights into actionable range and space recommendations that elevate the in-store fan experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Heads of Retail and General Managers to identify existing and new commercial opportunities that drive availability and satisfaction across all store grades.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feedback market intelligence and analysis to Buying &amp;amp; Merchandising teams to inform future ranging decisions and strengthen the end-to-end fan offer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation &amp;amp; Problem Solving&lt;/strong&gt; (Limitless Entrepreneurial Spirit)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trial and propose new ideas to move the business forward, including evolving allocation and replenishment systems for greater efficiency and accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage specific projects end-to-end — documenting and analysing information, formulating conclusions, and presenting recommendations to senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Potentialise sales and profit opportunities by store grade, using commercial analysis and data to unlock performance improvements across the estate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement best practice distribution methods in partnership with merchandising and supply chain teams, optimising delivery frequency and stock flow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/strong&gt; (Determined &amp;amp; Relentless Mindset)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set commercial initial allocations by category aligned with planned store turnover, space, and cover, and implement and manage the seasonal allocation and replenishment strategy by department and category.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse and review weekly, monthly, and seasonal trade by store and grade versus budget and prior year, proposing short, medium, and longer-term corrective actions with pace and precision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage store openings, modernisations, closures, and space changes in close collaboration with Buying &amp;amp; Merchandising teams to deliver successful launches on time and on brief.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the smooth flow of stock across stores, maximising potential through initial allocation, re-assortments, and end-of-season stock removal to Outlet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI &amp;amp; DIGITAL CAPABILITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building a future-ready organization. This role is expected to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply AI and technology to improve efficiency, quality, and outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data and digital tools to inform decisions and enhance performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate curiosity and adaptability in adopting new technologies and ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a culture of innovation and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CAPABILITIES &amp;amp; EXPERIENCE YOU BRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in a fast-paced Retail Merchandising or Space Planning role, ideally within a multi-site High Street or omnichannel retail environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial acumen with a deep understanding of store grading, range optimisation, space planning, and allocation and replenishment strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent numerical and analytical skills with the ability to interpret complex trading data and translate it into clear, actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence and communicate effectively at all levels, including gaining buy-in from Senior Management on strategic decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing store openings, closures, or estate changes in collaboration with buying, merchandising, and logistics functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, cross-functional working style with the ability to build effective relationships across retail, B&amp;amp;M, logistics, and finance teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and a solutions-focused mindset, with the ability to manage multiple priorities under pressure and deliver to deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WORK LOCATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hybrid: The primary place of performance of this role is the Company&#39;s office located in Manchester, subject to the Company&#39;s current hybrid work policy. This role currently requires in-office presence &lt;strong&gt;3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Fanatics, we operate with a BOLD mindset - We Build Championship Teams, we’re Obsessed with Fans, we embrace a Limitless Entrepreneurial Spirit, and we approach every challenge with a Determined and Relentless Mindset. If you’re ready to contribute to a dynamic, fast-paced environment that thrives on collaboration and growth, we want you to be part of our team.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;ABOUT US&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics Commerce is a leading designer, manufacturer, and seller of licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods. It operates a vertically-integrated platform of digital and physical capabilities for leading sports leagues, teams, colleges, and associations globally – as well as its flagship site, &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanatics.com&quot;&gt;www.fanatics.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics Commerce has a broad range of online, sports venue, and vertical apparel partnerships worldwide, including comprehensive partnerships with leading leagues, teams, colleges, and sports organizations across the world—including the NFL, NBA, MLB, NHL, MLS, Formula 1, and Australian Football League (AFL); the Dallas Cowboys, Golden State Warriors, Paris Saint-Germain, Chelsea FC, and Tokyo Giants; the University of Notre Dame, University of Alabama, and University of Texas; the International Olympic Committee (IOC), England Rugby, and the Union of European Football Associations (UEFA).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Fanatics Commerce, we infuse our BOLD Leadership Principles in everything we do:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;· Build Championship Teams&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;· Obsessed with Fans&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;· Limitless Entrepreneurial Spirit&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;· Determined and Relentless Mindset&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
